  "_comment": "Items this world can place. game_id is the MainManager.Items ordinal (the enum starts at None = -1), and kind is where it goes: 0 ordinary items, 1 key items, 2 medals (then game_id is the medal id, MainManager.BadgeTypes), 3 berries (money; game_id is the amount), 4 crystal berries (one item, game_id 0; the count is the currency; filler until the crystal berry shop is in the seed, then progression, since they buy locations there), 5 party members (game_id 0 Vi, 1 Kabbu, 2 Leif), 6 field abilities (game_id 0 Progressive Beemerang, 1 Horn Slash, 2 Progressive Freeze, 3 Jump, 4 Progressive Dash, 5 Bee Fly, 6 Beetle Dig, 7 Shield; the abilities by the game's own names, from its Skills text, and how many copies each takes, in abilities.py). The Archipelago id is ITEM_ID_BASE + game_id, plus MEDAL_ID_OFFSET for a medal (medal ids overlap item ids), MONEY_ID_OFFSET for berries, CRYSTAL_ID_OFFSET for crystal berries MEMBER_ID_OFFSET for a party member or MOVE_ID_OFFSET for a field move. padding marks the filler used to fill leftover locations, in any number; always marks an item that enters the pool once in every seed, taking a filler slot (the mod's own items, which no location holds in vanilla); member marks a party member, in the pool only with Starting Party Member on (the two not starting); move marks a field ability's item, in the pool as many times as abilities.py says (a base level the party starts with, with its option off, isn't one); every other item enters the pool once per included location that holds it in vanilla.",
